{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues\/refresh","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A refresh action stored in a view’s environment."}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"refresh"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"RefreshAction","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI13RefreshActionV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"role":"symbol","title":"refresh","externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI17EnvironmentValuesV7refreshAA13RefreshActionVSgvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property","extendedModule":"OpenSwiftUI","symbolKind":"property"},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"refresh"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI13RefreshActionV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"RefreshAction"},{"kind":"text","text":"? { "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"get"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"set"},{"kind":"text","text":" }"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When this environment value contains an instance of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" structure, certain built-in views in the corresponding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" begin offering a refresh capability. They apply the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"instance’s handler to any refresh operation that the user initiates.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"By default, the environment value is ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", but you can use the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"View\/refreshable(action:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" modifier to create and store a new","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"refresh action that uses the handler that you specify:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["List(mailbox.conversations) { conversation in","    ConversationCell(conversation)","}",".refreshable {","    await mailbox.fetch()","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On iOS and iPadOS, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"List"},{"type":"text","text":" in the example above offers a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"pull to refresh gesture because it detects the refresh action. When","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the user drags the list down and releases, the list calls the action’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"handler. Because OpenSwiftUI declares the handler as asynchronous, it can","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"safely make long-running asynchronous calls, like fetching network data.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Refreshing-Custom-Views","type":"heading","text":"Refreshing Custom Views","level":3},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can also offer refresh capability in your custom views.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Read the ","type":"text"},{"code":"refresh","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" environment value to get the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"instance for a given ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment","type":"reference"},{"text":". If you find","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a non-","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value, change your view’s appearance or behavior to offer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the refresh to the user, and call the instance to conduct the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"refresh. You can call the refresh instance directly because it defines"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction\/callAsFunction()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" method that Swift calls"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"when you call the instance:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct RefreshableView: View {","    @Environment(\\.refresh) private var refresh","","    var body: some View {","        Button(\"Refresh\") {","            Task {","                await refresh?()","            }","        }","        .disabled(refresh == nil)","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":null},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Be sure to call the handler asynchronously by preceding it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":". Because the call is asynchronous, you can use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its lifetime to indicate progress to the user. For example,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"you can reveal an indeterminate "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProgressView"},{"type":"text","text":" before"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"calling the handler, and hide it when the handler completes."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If your code isn’t already in an asynchronous context, create a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"doc:\/\/com.apple.documentation\/documentation\/Swift\/Task"},{"type":"text","text":" for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"method to run in. If you do this, consider adding a way for the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"user to cancel the task. For more information, see"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/docs.swift.org\/swift-book\/LanguageGuide\/Concurrency.html"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The Swift Programming Language"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/environmentvalues\/refresh"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/EnvironmentValues/refresh":{"fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"refresh","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI13RefreshActionV","text":"RefreshAction","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues\/refresh","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A refresh action stored in a view’s environment."}],"title":"refresh","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/environmentvalues\/refresh","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/RefreshAction":{"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/refreshaction","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction","title":"RefreshAction","role":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An action that initiates a refresh operation.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RefreshAction"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RefreshAction"}]},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/RefreshAction/callAsFunction()":{"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"callAsFunction","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/RefreshAction\/callAsFunction()","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Initiates a refresh action."}],"title":"callAsFunction()","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/refreshaction\/callasfunction()","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"https://docs.swift.org/swift-book/LanguageGuide/Concurrency.html":{"type":"link","title":"Concurrency","url":"https:\/\/docs.swift.org\/swift-book\/LanguageGuide\/Concurrency.html","identifier":"https:\/\/docs.swift.org\/swift-book\/LanguageGuide\/Concurrency.html","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Concurrency"}]},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/Environment":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/environment","title":"Environment","role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A property wrapper that reads a value from a view’s environment.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Environment","kind":"identifier"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Environment","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/EnvironmentValues":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EnvironmentValues"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/EnvironmentValues","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenSwiftUI exposes a collection of values to your app’s views in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EnvironmentValues"},{"type":"text","text":" structure. To read a value from the structure,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"declare a property using the "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Environment","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" property wrapper and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specify the value’s key path. For example, you can read the current locale:"}],"title":"EnvironmentValues","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/environmentvalues","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EnvironmentValues"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","role":"collection","abstract":[],"title":"OpenSwiftUI","url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"}}}